    "title": "Getting Fly for Humanity: Mission Waco Hosts Annual Fashion with a Passion - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nThe time is here! September 18th in the ballroom of the 1928 hotel will be the site of the Mission Waco Fashion with a Passion Style Show. Mission Waco is a non-profit that seeks to eliminate poverty in their own backyard. The fashion show proceeds go towards the creative arts program for the youth to provide them with a space to engage in musical and visual arts.\n“Usually we raise 30 to 40 thousand dollars, and we’re hoping to up that this year.” said Director of Events and Marketing, Megan Yingst-Coats. The entire Waco community comes together as many recognizable businesses support and participate in the event. This year they added another feature to the event that excited many as there were many raffles to be given away, from Baylor athletic tickets to purses and more.\nThe models were equally as excited for the event. There’s a mixture of first time walks and seasoned vets but they’re all ready to create a vibrant atmosphere for a good cause. The event is from 4:30 to 6:30 p.m. and if you’d like to support Mission Waco and attend, click here.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KWKT - FOX 44.\n2",
